{
  "id": "PPA-04",
  "title": "Cellular Respiration & Mitochondrial ETC",
  "subtitle": "Tricarboxylic acid cycle, classical respiratory complexes I-V, and plant-specific alternative bypasses",
  "caption": "Mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation and respiratory electron transport chain. Substrates derived from the TCA cycle feed electrons into classical Complex I (NADH DH) and Complex II (Succinate DH), as well as plant-specific rotenone-insensitive external/internal NAD(P)H dehydrogenases (NDA, NDB). Electrons funnel through ubiquinone to either classical Complex III/IV (generating a proton gradient for Complex V ATP synthase) or cyanide-resistant Alternative Oxidases (AOX1A/D), dissipating redox pressure as heat without proton translocation.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
